WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:127826

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.770
Let's now expand the agent collection by adding in another agent.

2
00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:07.774
This time, you'll use Google's Agent Development Kit, ADK,

3
00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:10.677
and Gemini 3 Pro on Vertex AI.

4
00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:13.179
This agent will perform research using Google search

5
00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:16.383
about a user's health conditions and provide the results.

6
00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:20.687
ADK and several other frameworks have built-in integrations with A2A,

7
00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:23.890
which makes it much easier to make agents A2A compliant.

8
00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:25.692
So that's what we'll be using

9
00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.460
for this agent. Let's get to it.

10
00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:29.796
Let's write the code for the research agent.

11
00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.799
This agent will run Google search

12
00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:35.602
and present research about health conditions to the end user.

13
00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:38.104
I'm saving this code as a Python file again,

14
00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:41.107
this time called a2a_research_agent.py.

15
00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:44.110
I'll import some libraries, including

16
00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:47.414
Agent Development Kit and the to_a2a method.

17
00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:50.950
I'll disable warnings because this library tends to be pretty noisy

18
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.752
when using A2A as it's experimental.

19
00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.955
I'll load in environment variables and authenticate to Google Cloud.

20
00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:59.259
Next, I'll load the host and port from the environment.

21
00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:00.960
Note, the port is going to

22
00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.829
be different from the insurance policy agent

23
00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:05.932
because they need to be running simultaneously on the same system.

24
00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:08.435
Now, I'll define the ADK agent.

25
00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:12.072
In this case, it'll be an LLMAgent,

26
00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:14.474
which I'll call research agent.

27
00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:18.078
I'll provide the model ID, gemini-3-pro-preview,

28
00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:20.480
and give it the name HealthResearchAgent.

29
00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.782
I'll add some tools.

30
00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.951
In this case, we will use Gemini's built-in Google

31
00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:27.087
search tool within ADK to help with the research.

32
00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:29.089
I'll add a description of this agent.

33
00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:32.792
provides healthcare information about symptoms, health conditions, treatments, and procedures.

34
00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.662
using up-to-date web resources.

35
00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:39.466
And I'll give the system instructions, telling it to research health conditions.

36
00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:42.068
Next, I'll create the main method.

37
00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:45.371
All you need to do to make this agent A2A-compatible

38
00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:47.373
is call the to_a2a method.

39
00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:50.376
Pass in the agent, the host, and port,

40
00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:53.379
and then pass this a2a_app to uvicorn run

41
00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:57.183
to run it. You don't have to create agent cards or agent

42
00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:00.253
executors, because ADK has already written the code for you.

43
00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:03.957
ADK uses the agent name, tools, and description

44
00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:06.059
to fill out the agent card and skills.

45
00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:07.494
Now, I'm going to go ahead

46
00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:08.962
and run this code in terminal two.

47
00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:14.062
So, I'll type in uv run a2a_research_agent.py.

48
00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:16.302
Now that you have this agent running, you have a

49
00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:18.071
lot of options for what you can do with it.

50
00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:21.074
You can reuse the client that we created in the previous lesson.

51
00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:23.776
It's already set up to work with this type of agent.

52
00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:27.347
Just use a different query and a different host and port,

53
00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:30.049
and you can access it the exact same way as before.

54
00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.985
Note that this agent will respond with

55
00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:33.553
a task instead of an immediate message,

56
00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:35.355
so that client will handle it slightly

57
00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:37.056
differently than the previous agent we created.

58
00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:39.459
Or you can do what we'll do in the next lesson,

59
00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:42.128
where we'll combine this agent with the previous agent

60
00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.430
to create a sequential workflow.
